#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_irreducible_polynomial

#% text
# `is_irreducible_polynomial(f)` gives `true` when the polynomial `f` cannot be written as a product of two polynomials of lower degree with rational coefficients.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `is_irreducible_polynomial(f, modulus: p)` tests irreducibility over the integers modulo the prime `p`, and `is_irreducible_polynomial(f, extension: F)` over the finite field `F`; a polynomial with finite field elements as coefficients is tested over their field.

#% item
# Constants are not irreducible. Over the rationals `f` is factored; over a finite field it is factored there.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_irreducible_polynomial(x^4 + 1)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_irreducible_polynomial(x^4 + 1, modulus: 3)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Over an extension field:

#% cell
is_irreducible_polynomial(x^2 + x + 1, extension: finite_field(2, 2))
#% output
#= false

#% text
# Several variables:

#% cell
is_irreducible_polynomial(x^2 - y^2)
#% output
#= false

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `factor`, `is_primitive_polynomial`, `conway_polynomial`
